@startuml evidence-panel
title US-14: Evidence Panel - Why the Alert Fired, Assembled from All Three Stores

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

participant "Express API" as API
database "Redis\nentity:live:{id}" as Redis
database "TimescaleDB\nalerts + position_history" as TSDB
database "Neo4j\nentity graph" as Neo4j
participant "Angular\nDashboard" as Dashboard
actor Operator

note over API
  Operator opens the evidence panel for a COMPOSITE alert.
  API fetches from all three stores in parallel
  to assemble the full picture.
end note

par fetch current state
  API -> Redis : HGETALL entity:live:VesselB
  Redis --> API : { lat, lon, last_seen_ms } or nil (still dark)
else fetch alert record and position history
  API -> TSDB : SELECT * FROM alerts WHERE alert_id = $1
  TSDB --> API : { alert_type: COMPOSITE, payload: { signal_loss_duration_ms,\n  proximity_entity_id, proximity_distance_metres } }
else fetch relationship context
  API -> Neo4j : MATCH (b:Entity {id: 'VesselB'})\nOPTIONAL MATCH (b)-[k:KNOWN_ASSOCIATE]-(known)\nOPTIONAL MATCH (b)-[p:PROXIMITY_EVENT]-(recent)\nWHERE p.timestamp_ms > $window_start\nRETURN known, recent
  Neo4j --> API : known associates, recent proximity events
end

note over API
  Each store answers a different question:
  Redis:     "Is the entity still dark right now?"
  TSDB:      "What rule fired and what were the thresholds?"
  Neo4j:     "Is this proximity entity known or unrelated?"
  No single store answers all three.
end note

API --> Dashboard : evidence panel payload\n{ current_state, alert_detail,\n  known_associates, proximity_events,\n  composite_score }

Dashboard --> Operator : evidence panel rendered\n- signal loss duration\n- proximity entity (flagged as unknown)\n- last known position on map\n- which thresholds were crossed

@enduml
